(6768666, 1013509, 67152, '<td valign="top">a decent idea for the challenge - but the processing is overcooked so that all detail in the bottles is lost - and the overall image is so incredibly busy with the sudoku in the background, the many colors on the bottles.   Because it is cluttered, it doesn''t seem to feel empty, rather full of empties.</td>', 'a decent idea for the challenge - but the processing is overcooked so that all detail in the bottles is lost - and the overall image is so incredibly busy with the sudoku in the background, the many colors on the bottles.   Because it is cluttered, it doesn''t seem to feel empty, rather full of empties.', '2012-05-14 09:07:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6768677, 1013509, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> a decent idea for the challenge - but the processing is overcooked so that all detail in the bottles is lost - and the overall image is so incredibly busy with the sudoku in the background, the many colors on the bottles.   Because it is cluttered, it doesn''t seem to feel empty, rather full of empties. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks bassbone - I realise I had totally overlooked the fact that a screen full of bottles is so clearly not empty and for this reason alone I think I was lucky to score as highly as I did. Doh!!! I do tend to get carried away with over-processing quite often to try and disguise a very average looking photo:)</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone: a decent idea for the challenge - but the processing is overcooked so that all detail in the bottles is lost - and the overall image is so incredibly busy with the sudoku in the background, the many colors on the bottles.   Because it is cluttered, it doesn''t seem to feel empty, rather full of empties.   Thanks bassbone - I realise I had totally overlooked the fact that a screen full of bottles is so clearly not empty and for this reason alone I think I was lucky to score as highly as I did. Doh!!! I do tend to get carried away with over-processing quite often to try and disguise a very average looking photo:)', '2012-05-14 09:29:17.000000', NULL, 0),
